import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Corrections" description="Sublime Pantry's public corrections log. When we get something wrong, the fix is recorded here." path="/corrections" breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Corrections", href: "/corrections" }]}>
  <span class="kicker">Policy</span>
  <h1>Corrections</h1>
  <p>When we publish an error of fact, we correct the article, add a correction note to it, and record the correction here with the date. Style fixes and minor copy edits are not logged; factual corrections always are.</p>
  <h2>Log</h2>
  <ol class="corrections-log">
    <li>
      <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-09-06">September 6, 2026</time> — <a href="/compare/home-freeze-dryers">Home freeze dryers compared</a></p>
      <p><strong>Pump type stated incorrectly.</strong> Criterion 4 described the Harvest
      Right Premier as an oil-free pump and said it removed routine oil changes
      entirely. The Premier is an oil pump; oil-free is a priced upgrade on Harvest
      Right's own bundle listing. The Premier lengthens the oil-change interval — a
      change and filtering every 20-30 batches, against every 4-5 on the standard
      pump — rather than eliminating it.</p>
      <p>The error was a maintenance-cost misstatement material to a purchase
      decision, and it contradicted our own buying guide, which had the pump type
      right. Criterion 4 has been rewritten and the article carries a correction
      note. Found during an internal messaging audit, not reported by a reader.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>Spotted an error? <a href="/contact">Report it</a> — we take these seriously and respond to every report.</p>
</PageLayout>
